Cell 2: Synthetic Test Pattern and Visual Validation
Paste this into the second cell to stream a high-contrast geometry pattern through the DMA engine and plot the detected corner coordinates inline:
# Configure dimensions (VGA 640x480)
WIDTH = 640
HEIGHT = 480

# 1. Program HLS AXI-Lite registers
harris_ip.register_map.rows = HEIGHT
harris_ip.register_map.cols = WIDTH
harris_ip.register_map.threshold = 442
harris_ip.register_map.k_scaled = 2621  # 0.04 scaled in fixed-point

# 2. Allocate contiguous physical memory
in_buf = allocate(shape=(HEIGHT, WIDTH), dtype=np.uint8)
out_buf = allocate(shape=(HEIGHT, WIDTH), dtype=np.uint8)

# 3. Create a synthetic test image with crisp corners
test_img = np.zeros((HEIGHT, WIDTH), dtype=np.uint8)
# Add a white central rectangle
test_img[120:360, 160:480] = 255
# Add a smaller dark box inside to create 8 total corners
test_img[180:300, 240:400] = 0
np.copyto(in_buf, test_img)

# 4. Arm the receive channel FIRST (prevents AXI-Stream pipeline deadlock)
dma.recvchannel.transfer(out_buf)

# 5. Start the HLS IP core
harris_ip.register_map.CTRL.AP_START = 1

# 6. Stream input pixels through DMA send channel
t0 = time.time()
dma.sendchannel.transfer(in_buf)

# 7. Wait for both DMA transfers to complete
dma.sendchannel.wait()
dma.recvchannel.wait()
t1 = time.time()

fpga_latency_ms = (t1 - t0) * 1000.0
detected_corners = np.count_nonzero(out_buf == 255)

print(f"FPGA Roundtrip Time: {fpga_latency_ms:.2f} ms")
print(f"Detected Corner Points: {detected_corners}")

# 8. Plot input vs detected corners side-by-side
fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 5))

ax[0].imshow(in_buf, cmap='gray')
ax[0].set_title("Input Synthetic Image (640x480)")
ax[0].axis('off')

# Overlay detected corners (red markers) on the grayscale image
ax[1].imshow(in_buf, cmap='gray')
y_coords, x_coords = np.where(out_buf == 255)
ax[1].scatter(x_coords, y_coords, color='red', s=30, label='Hardware Corner')
ax[1].set_title(f"FPGA Harris Output ({detected_corners} corners)")
ax[1].legend(loc="upper right")
ax[1].axis('off')

plt.tight_layout()
plt.show()

# 9. Free memory allocations
in_buf.freebuffer()
out_buf.freebuffer()

 * Verification: A two-panel plot appears showing red scatter points clustered at the corners of the shapes, and the execution completes in under 15 ms.
